      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__edge__setters_1ga11436b83042ee2c3812bd4b7fc42e3ea" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>const int</type>
        <definition>const int ndxlSetEdgeParams</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLEdge *_Edge, void *_Params)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlSetEdgeParams</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1aa30ac2f40da4dbe7d841088a78f957fe" kindref="member">NDXLEdge</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Edge</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>void *</type>
          <declname>_Params</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Sets the user-defined <computeroutput>void* _Params</computeroutput> of an edge. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Edge</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target edge to update the parameters of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Params</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to extra memory used by the edge. May be NULL.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If _Edge is NULL, returns <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>, otherwise updates the parameters of _Edge, and returns NDXL_OK.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>NDXL stores the supplied <computeroutput>void* _Params</computeroutput> pointer without copying the associated data or managing its lifetime. The pointed-to memory must remain valid for as long as the edge uses it.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>This function replaces the edge&apos;s existing parameter pointer without freeing or otherwise managing the memory it previously referenced. The user remains responsible for managing both the previous and new allocations.</para>
</simplesect>
